3. Phase 2 — canonical noun extraction (first pass)
============================================================
Wrote Greek_Noun_Extraction_NIM/rebuild_noun_occurrences_ot.py, modeled on the
existing NT extractor (rebuild_noun_occurrences_from_strongs.py) with Hebrew-specific
adaptations:

  - Source: strongs_ot WHERE morph LIKE 'N%' (both Nc* common and Np* proper nouns,
    per the approved Phase 2 plan — proper nouns counted, flagged by category)
  - nouns table keyed by Strong's H-number -> Hebrew dictionary headword lemma
    (NOT inflected surface form), language_code = 'hbo'
  - Hebrew Strong's dictionary parsed via Node.js require() + JSON.stringify()
    (Python's json.loads() failed on JS-only \' escapes) -> /tmp/strongs_hebrew.json,
    8,674 entries (lemma, xlit, pron, derivation, strongs_def, kjv_def)
  - infer_category_id(): keyword buckets against strongs_def gloss text — PLACE,
    TIME, MONEY, BODY_PART, FOOD, ANIMAL; hard-coded GOD_LEMMAS set for
    Elohim/El/YHWH/Adonai/Shaddai; Np* defaults to PERSON unless gloss says
    otherwise; else OTHER
  - surface_form = strongs_ot.word with '/' morphological separators stripped
    (no beta-code transliteration needed — XML already gives pointed Unicode)

